{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0162d14d094e00b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n3\ttitle: GA-readiness assessment for Llama Stack\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 1\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# GA-readiness assessment for Llama Stack\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis epic resolves the strategy's central unknown: no systematic GA-readiness\n30\tassessment of Llama Stack has been done, and TP feedback is scattered across\n31\tsupport tickets. The assessment inventories the gaps between current Tech\n32\tPreview quality and the GA bar across API stability, upgrade paths, scale\n33\tlimits, and error handling, and produces the definitive GA scope that the\n34\tstability and hardening work is planned from. Until this assessment lands, the\n35\tsize of the graduation work is only an estimate.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Inventory API stability gaps on the published API surface (current\n40\t  versioning state, unintentional breaking changes between TP releases,\n41\t  deprecation exposure).\n42\t- Assess the upgrade paths from the last two TP releases, identifying breaks\n43\t  and missing migration steps.\n44\t- Identify scale limits (concurrency, throughput, resource ceilings) relative\n45\t  to the GA bar.\n46\t- Assess error handling coverage and behavior on the published surfaces.\n47\t- Consolidate TP feedback scattered across support tickets and validate it\n48\t  against the current codebase.\n49\t- Produce the definitive GA scope: an enumerated gap inventory with severity,\n50\t  each gap classified as GA-blocking or deferrable, with a recommended\n51\t  remediation approach at a level the implementing team can plan from.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- A GA-readiness report exists covering all four enumerated dimensions (API\n56\t  stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling), each with\n57\t  enumerated, specific findings.\n58\t- TP feedback from support tickets is consolidated and either confirmed\n59\t  against the codebase or explicitly marked unconfirmed.\n60\t- A definitive GA scope is produced that classifies every identified gap as\n61\t  GA-blocking or deferrable.\n62\t- Every GA-blocking gap carries a recommended remediation approach sufficient\n63\t  for implementation planning.\n64\t- The report distinguishes measured/verified findings from reported-but-\n65\t  unconfirmed ones.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-1 (P0): \"A GA-readiness assessment inventories the gaps between current\n70\t  TP quality and GA bar (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error\n71\t  handling), producing the definitive GA scope.\" This epic is that assessment.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9087eabab116ac81","agent_id":"a92865f3bd55d505c","session_id":"30fb2c83-c81f-4c8e-a80f-08c43025fc68","uuid":"11dcd2be-b0db-41da-9473-cfd21f52e135","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:12:21.434Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0162d14d094e00b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
