ma Stack API surface.\n50\t- Define the deprecation policy covering the published API surface, authored\n51\t  together with the versioning scheme it governs.\n52\t- Build and test the upgrade path from each of the last two TP releases.\n53\t- Remediate the GA-blocking findings of the GA-readiness assessment (error\n54\t  handling, scale limits, and other assessment-identified gaps), per the\n55\t  definitive GA scope.\n56\t- Keep the existing Konflux build pipeline green throughout.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- The published APIs are versioned and the versioning scheme is documented.\n61\t- A deprecation policy covering the published API surface is defined and\n62\t  published.\n63\t- Upgrade from each of the last two TP releases is exercised by automated\n64\t  tests and passes.\n65\t- Every GA-blocking finding from the GA-readiness assessment is remediated,\n66\t  or explicitly deferred with recorded rationale in the GA scope.\n67\t- The existing Konflux build pipeline remains green with all changes.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- HLR-2 (P0): \"Published API surface carries a stability guarantee: versioned\n72\t  APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last two TP\n73\t  releases.\" The deprecation policy is authored here rather than in the\n74\t  documentation epic because it is part of the same stability-guarantee\n75\t  deliverable on the same API surface — the policy expresses the versioning\n76\t  decisions this epic makes.\n77\t- Implements the remediation half of HLR-1's output: the GA-blocking findings\n78\t  from the GA-readiness assessment are closed here.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9087eabab116ac81","agent_id":"a92865f3bd55d505c","session_id":"30fb2c83-c81f-4c8e-a80f-08c43025fc68","uuid":"a4a7622d-dc9a-4442-9f25-78f4a17c749d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:12:22.059Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-892a98e5249374ae","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config",