nt surfaces in the Dashboard\n53\t  with no user opt-in action.\n54\t- On a non-entitled cluster, Llama Stack management surfaces are not enabled.\n55\t- The default enablement is controlled through the Dashboard's existing\n56\t  configuration mechanism so it can be reverted without code changes\n57\t  (rollback for the replaced opt-in-gate behavior).\n58\t- The existing Dashboard test suite and build pipeline remain green.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- HLR-5 (P1): \"The Dashboard enables Llama Stack management by default for\n63\t  entitled clusters (no TP opt-in gate).\"\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9087eabab116ac81","agent_id":"a92865f3bd55d505c","session_id":"30fb2c83-c81f-4c8e-a80f-08c43025fc68","uuid":"4cc89b61-ab57-4f63-b445-b24b2ef5c4ac","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:12:23.331Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a59d58c03c1c02c3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
