{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b37ffbaf8786baa4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9014\n3\ttitle: Graduate Llama Stack to General Availability\n4\tstatus: Refinement Done\n5\tpriority: Critical\n6\tlabels:\n7\t- refined\n8\t- genai\n9\tlinks: []\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t## Problem Statement\n13\t\n14\tLlama Stack shipped as Tech Preview and adoption is strong, but enterprise\n15\tcustomers will not build production GenAI applications on a TP component.\n16\tGraduating to GA requires API stability commitments, a production support\n17\tposture, and closing the quality gaps that TP status currently excuses. The\n18\tfull inventory of those gaps is not yet known — TP feedback is scattered across\n19\tsupport tickets, and no systematic GA-readiness assessment has been done.\n20\t\n21\t## High-Level Requirements\n22\t\n23\t| ID | Priority | Requirement |\n24\t|-------|----------|-------------|\n25\t| HLR-1 | P0 | A GA-readiness assessment inventories the gaps between current TP quality and GA bar (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling), producing the definitive GA scope. |\n26\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Published API surface carries a stability guarantee: versioned APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last two TP releases. |\n27\t| HLR-3 | P0 | Production support posture is in place: documented SLO targets, backport policy, and supported configuration matrix. |\n28\t| HLR-4 | P1 | Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions. |\n29\t| HLR-5 | P1 | The Dashboard enables Llama Stack management by default for entitled clusters (no TP opt-in gate). |\n30\t| HLR-6 | P2 | Documentation is uplifted to GA standards, including migration notes from TP. |\n31\t\n32\t## Affected Components\n33\t\n34\t- Llama Stack\n35\t- TrustyAI\n36\t- Dashboard\n37\t\n38\t## Out of Scope\n39\t\n40\t- New Llama Stack feature development beyond GA-bar quality work\n41\t- Deprecating alternative GenAI serving paths\n42\t\n43\t## Open Questions\n44\t\n45\t1. The GA scope itself depends on HLR-1's assessment — until it lands, the\n46\t   size of the stability and hardening work is an estimate.\n47\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e07987742a7e0e3","agent_id":"a782a49403a33104d","session_id":"30fb2c83-c81f-4c8e-a80f-08c43025fc68","uuid":"84186c01-03e3-4279-b856-ea66ac5b6279","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:15:41.057Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b37ffbaf8786baa4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014"}
