ation is part of the integration deliverable (it\n50\t  defines what \"supported\" means for this integration); it is distinct from\n51\t  the broader Llama Stack GA documentation uplift.\n52\t- Coordinate with the Llama Stack distribution owners on enablement defaults\n53\t  for GA distributions.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- The guardrails integration is available in GA Llama Stack distributions\n58\t  without an experimental opt-in flag.\n59\t- The integration is validated end-to-end against a Llama Stack distribution,\n60\t  including error and misconfiguration behavior, with results recorded.\n61\t- Documentation for the supported integration exists, covering configuration,\n62\t  capabilities, and support boundaries.\n63\t- The supported integration can be disabled via supported configuration\n64\t  without code changes (rollback for the replaced experimental-flag behavior).\n65\t- The existing build pipeline for the changed repositories remains green.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-4 (P1): \"Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n70\t  integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions.\"\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e07987742a7e0e3","agent_id":"a782a49403a33104d","session_id":"30fb2c83-c81f-4c8e-a80f-08c43025fc68","uuid":"a5be31eb-d43a-4c40-8fcf-1e3344f15413","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:15:47.605Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3befa5a15d94405","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014"}
