{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-837c43131e896487","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E004\n3\ttitle: Dashboard Llama Stack management enabled by default for entitled clusters\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Dashboard Llama Stack management enabled by default for entitled clusters\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic removes the Tech Preview opt-in gate so that the Dashboard enables\n34\tLlama Stack management by default on entitled clusters. Today the management\n35\texperience sits behind a TP opt-in; for GA it becomes a default-on,\n36\tentitlement-gated capability.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Change the Dashboard's Llama Stack management default from opt-in to\n41\t  enabled, using the Dashboard's existing per-component feature-flag and\n42\t  defaults configuration mechanism.\n43\t- Remove the Tech Preview opt-in gate for Llama Stack management.\n44\t- Gate the default enablement on cluster entitlement: enabled on entitled\n45\t  clusters, hidden or disabled elsewhere.\n46\t- Update captions, labels, and references that fall out of this change (e.g.,\n47\t  removing TP designations on the management surfaces) — incidental touch-ups\n48\t  only, no new content authored here.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- On an entitled cluster, Llama Stack management surfaces in the Dashboard\n53\t  with no user opt-in action.\n54\t- On a non-entitled cluster, Llama Stack management surfaces are not enabled.\n55\t- The default enablement is controlled through the Dashboard's existing\n56\t  configuration mechanism so it can be reverted without code changes\n57\t  (rollback for the replaced opt-in-gate behavior).\n58\t- The existing Dashboard test suite and build pipeline remain green.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- HLR-5 (P1): \"The Dashboard enables Llama Stack management by default for\n63\t  entitled clusters (no TP opt-in gate).\"\n64\t\n65\t## Notes\n66\t\n67\t- **Release-timing coordination:** the default-on management experience is\n68\t  intended to ship as part of the Llama Stack GA graduation, not before it.\n69\t  This is a release-composition matter — coordinate the release timing of\n70\t  this change with the Llama Stack GA release planning so the default-on\n71\t  Dashboard experience lands with (not ahead of) the GA graduation. It is\n72\t  deliberately not a DAG dependency: this epic's implementation is complete\n73\t  and independently testable regardless of GA timing, so it blocks on\n74\t  nothing and only the GA documentation epic consumes its outcome.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e07987742a7e0e3","agent_id":"a782a49403a33104d","session_id":"30fb2c83-c81f-4c8e-a80f-08c43025fc68","uuid":"fcdb8cef-fa3d-4142-a016-8a5e6d1d9650","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:15:48.236Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-837c43131e896487","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014"}
